#!/usr/bin/python3
# fp5-hfp-modem-bridge — let a Bluetooth car kit (HFP Hands-Free) dial, answer
# and hang up VoLTE calls on the FP5 (BengalOS), and carry call audio over SCO.
#
# PipeWire's native HFP Audio Gateway only knows ModemManager's Voice API. On
# the FP5, calls are made by imsd (userspace IMS) through imsd-ofonod, an
# oFono-compatible VoiceCallManager; ModemManager never sees them. This daemon
# owns its own bus name and exposes a ModemManager-shaped modem whose Voice /
# Call objects mirror imsd-ofonod's calls. A patched libspa-bluez5 is pointed
# at it with
#   bluez5.hfphsp-backend-native-modem         = "fp5-imsd"
#   bluez5.hfphsp-backend-native-modem-service = "io.github.isyourbrainfoss.Fp5HfpModem"
# (an unpatched PipeWire ignores the service key and, since no real modem has
# Device "fp5-imsd", links to nothing: same as today.)
#
# Dial policy (VoLTE first, CS when needed):
#   IMS usable (imsd-ofonod modem Online)  -> imsd Dial
#     imsd Dial fails fast (error < FAST_FAIL_S, no call object) and CS usable
#                                           -> ModemManager Voice.CreateCall + Call.Start (CS)
#   IMS not usable, CS usable               -> ModemManager CS call
#   neither                                 -> error (car shows no service)
# CS usable = real ModemManager modem registered, has Voice, not EmergencyOnly.
# CS calls (ours, gnome-calls' or incoming) are mirrored like imsd calls.
#
# Car -> phone:  ATD -> Voice.CreateCall -> org.ofono VoiceCallManager.Dial
#                ATA -> Call.Accept      -> VoiceCall.Answer
#                AT+CHUP -> Call.Hangup  -> VoiceCall.Hangup
#                AT+VTS  -> Call.SendDtmf -> VoiceCallManager.SendTones
# Phone -> car:  oFono CallAdded/PropertyChanged/CallRemoved -> MM CallAdded /
#                Call.StateChanged / CallDeleted (PipeWire turns those into
#                +CIEV, RING/+CLIP and +CLCC).
# Service/signal/operator/roaming indicators mirror the real ModemManager
# (read-only). IMEI and own numbers are never exposed. Logs never contain
# phone numbers.
#
# Optional audio routing (fp5_hfp_audio.py): while a call exists and a car is
# connected, switch its card to the HFP profile and make its SCO sink and
# WirePlumber's SCO loopback source the defaults (imsd-media plays with pw-play
# and records with pw-record when media starts, so it opens on them). For a
# car-dialled call this happens BEFORE imsd Dial. No mid-call re-assert; one
# move at most for a stream found off the car. Restore A2DP + defaults +
# unmute afterwards, also after a crash.
#
# v3 (car test 2026-11-20 16:04):
# - car mic volume floor in fp5_hfp_audio (the car's HFP input route was 0%).
# - gnome-calls refresh: gnome-calls 51.1's oFono provider forgets the origin
#   when org.ofono vanishes but keeps the modem in its table, so when
#   imsd-ofonod comes back ("Modem `/imsd' already exists") calls are added
#   to a dead origin: no call UI (16:04, assertion G_IS_DBUS_CONNECTION) or a
#   calls-daemon SEGV (08:40, 09:15, 12:27). imsd-ofonod restarts many times a
#   day. After it comes back and no call is live, `systemctl --user
#   try-restart calls-daemon` (FP5_CALLS_REFRESH=off to disable). Also at
#   start-up if the running gnome-calls already logged "Ofono vanished".
# - diagnostics: log once when PipeWire reads a call's state, and log car
#   commands for unknown call objects (car hangup at 16:05 left no trace).
